This looks like a finished meal. The plate holds only a banana peel, so there is essentially no food left. The bowl has a few crumbs or residue, the glass has a trace of liquid, and the milk bottle is empty.

The peel itself is not food energy, so I counted only the residue. A few crumbs in the bowl might be about 2 g, and the trace of liquid in the glass adds almost nothing. That gives roughly 5 kcal and 3 g.

